IT359 Project Plan
Overview:
Project Name: AI Security Analyst - Sn00py Bl0ck3r
Project Description: Sn00py Bl0ck3r is an AI-assisted cybersecurity analysis tool designed to help users identify potential inbound security threats. The application will analyze QR codes, URLs, emails, files, downloads, and files obtained from removable USB storage for indicators of phishing or malicious activity.
Sn00py Bl0ck3r will combine rule-based security checks, reputation services, file and URL analysis, and AI-generated explanations to provide users with a clear risk score and a human-readable summary of why an item may be considered suspicious.
The goal is not to replace antivirus or enterprise security software, but to create an easy-to-use security analysis tool that helps users better understand potential threats before interacting with suspicious content.
Objectives and Success Criteria:
-	Develop a functioning cybersecurity analysis application 
-	Analyze URLs for suspicious characteristics and reputation information
-	Decode and analyze QR codes before users visit the embedded URL
-	Analyze email content and available header information for phishing indicators.
-	Analyze files using file type, metadata, cryptographic hashes, and reputation information
-	Allow files from removable USB devices to be selected and analyzed
-	Generate an overall risk score for analyzed items
-	Provide a human-readable explanation of detected risks
-	Maintain a record or dashboard of completed scans and results
-	Provide clear documentation explaining installation and usage
Will be considered successful if:
-	The application successfully analyzed at least four supported threat categories 
-	QR codes can be decoded and their URLs analyzed
-	Suspicious URLs and email indicators can be identified using defined security rules.
-	Files can be analyzed without being executed
-	The system produces consistent risk scores such as Low, Medium, High, or Critical
-	Users receive an understandable explanation of why an item received its score
-	The program can successfully demonstrate both safe and suspicious test samples
-	The application operates without major crashes during final testing and demonstration
-	All required GitHub, report, and presentation deliverables are completed by the final deadline
