Risk Management

Risk - Project scope becomes too large	Probability - High	Impact - High	Mitigation - Prioritize core features and treat additional features as optional enhancements
Risk - External API becomes unavailable 	Probability - Medium	Impact - High	Mitigation - Design local analysis features that can operate without the API and identify backup services where possible
Risk - API rate limits are reached	Probability - Medium	Impact - Medium	Mitigation - Cache results when appropriate and limit unnecessary API requests
Risk - False positives/False negativites 	Probability - High	Impact - Medium	Mitigation - Use multiple indicators and clearly state that results are advisory
Risk - AI produces inaccurate explanation	Probability - Medium	Impact - Medium	Mitigation - Based the risk score primarily on measurable security indicators rather than AI output alone
Risk - Malware or unsafe file handling	Probability - Low	Impact - High	Mitigation - Use static analysis only and never intentionally execute malicious files
Risk - Integration problems between modules	Probability - Medium	Impact - High	Mitigation - Integrate components throughout development rather than waiting until the end
Risk - GitHub merge conflicts or lost work	Probability - Medium	Impact - Medium	Mitigation - Use branches, frequent commits, and pull requests where appropriate
Risk - Team member availability 	Probability - Medium	Impact - Medium	Mitigation - Maintain shared documentation and avoid assigning an entire critical system to only one person
Risk - Development falls behind schedule	Probability - Medium	Impact - High	Mitigation - Review progress weekly and reduce optional features when necessary
Risk - Demo failure	Low-Medium	Probability - High Impact - N/A	Mitigation - Prepare tested demonstration samples and complete multiple practice run before recording
Risk - Internet failure during demo	Probability - Low	Impact - Medium	Mitigation - Include examples that can demonstrate local analysis without requiring live API connections

